-- LAYER-1 TESTS: the Revised Edition 2000's ss 34, 35 and 36 (sgta-part6-2000ed.l4).
-- Two kinds of expectation.  (1) The same hand-written expectations as sgta-tests-part6-part8.l4 gives for ss 54, 55 and 56, because the words are the same except in drafting form
-- (TA1999.20001230.txt:1246-1287 against TA1999.txt:4894-4947).  (2) A grid of inputs on which each 2000 Edition function must give the very answer the 2020 function gives: the grid is every
-- combination of three pieces of equipment, six holdings and the Boolean facts, so a change to either text's rule that made the two differ would turn a line red.  (3) The dispatchers, which pick
-- the text each version prints.

§ `Test equipment and holdings`

`a walkie-talkie` MEANS `A piece of equipment` OF "a hand-held walkie-talkie", (LIST `transmission`, `reception`), (LIST `Hertzian or radio waves`)
`a wired telephone` MEANS `A piece of equipment` OF "a wired telephone", (LIST `transmission`, `reception`), (LIST `wire`)
`a GPS receiver` MEANS `A piece of equipment` OF "a GPS receiver", (LIST `reception`), (LIST `Hertzian or radio waves`)

`holds nothing` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a section 5 licence` MEANS `What the person holds` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a regulatory authorisation` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a Minister's exemption` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a treaty licence` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`holds a Broadcasting Act licence` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

`the general penalty` MEANS `Penalty` OF 10000, 36, 1000, TRUE

§ `s 34 of the 2000 Edition, by hand`

#ASSERT `s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a GPS receiver` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` TRUE `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a section 5 licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a regulatory authorisation`))
-- the exception names only a s 5 licence and regulations; exemption and treaty licence are in ss 36 and 73 of the 2000 Edition, not in s 34(1)
#ASSERT `s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a Minister's exemption`
#ASSERT `s 34(1)(b) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a treaty licence`
#ASSERT `s 34(1)(a) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 34(1)(a) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 34(1)(a) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` TRUE `holds a section 5 licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 34(1)(a) of the 2000 Edition: the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` FALSE `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT `s 34(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` `holds a section 5 licence`
#ASSERT `s 34(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` `holds a regulatory authorisation`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 34(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` `holds nothing`))
-- s 34(2) outcome.  argument order: equipment, offers for sale, possesses, holds, "regulation of a system required for broadcasting", is broadcasting apparatus
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the general penalty`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a section 5 licence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a Minister's exemption` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a treaty licence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a wired telephone` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading B of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` EQUALS `an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the general penalty`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading B of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a section 5 licence` EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 34(2) of the 2000 Edition: the outcome, on Reading A of s 72 (s 95 today)` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the general penalty`

§ `s 35 and s 36 of the 2000 Edition, by hand`

#ASSERT `s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a vehicle in Singapore` `holds nothing`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a section 5 licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a regulatory authorisation`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a Minister's exemption`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a treaty licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a wired telephone` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(1) of the 2000 Edition: the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE `in a place in Singapore` `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT `s 35(2) of the 2000 Edition: the person is deemed to have operated it` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(2) of the 2000 Edition: the person is deemed to have operated it` TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(2) of the 2000 Edition: the person is deemed to have operated it` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 35(3) of the 2000 Edition: the occupier is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(3) of the 2000 Edition: the occupier is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(3) of the 2000 Edition: the occupier is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(3) of the 2000 Edition: the occupier is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 35(4) of the 2000 Edition: the defence is made out` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(4) of the 2000 Edition: the defence is made out` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35(4) of the 2000 Edition: the defence is made out` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `s 36 of the 2000 Edition: sections 33, 34 and 35 do not apply to the person (subject to the Authority's conditions)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 36 of the 2000 Edition: sections 33, 34 and 35 do not apply to the person (subject to the Authority's conditions)` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 36 of the 2000 Edition: sections 33, 34 and 35 do not apply to the person (subject to the Authority's conditions)` FALSE TRUE))

